{% comment %}
  Product page sound button - click to play only, never autoplay.
  Maps the product to a category clip via its primary collection, with a
  per-product override through the "custom.sound_clip" metafield (single
  line text - the filename under assets/sounds/, e.g. "hing-grind.mp3").

  Until real recorded/licensed clips are supplied, assets/vishesh-sound.js
  plays a short generated tone instead (see the STUB flag in that file) -
  this button and its markup do not change when real audio ships, only
  the JS stops stubbing.

  Accepts: product (required)
{% endcomment %}

{%- if settings.sound_button_enable and product != blank -%}
  {%- assign sound_key = 'default' -%}
  {%- assign primary_handle = product.collections.first.handle -%}
  {%- assign known_categories = 'asafoetida-hing,authentic-blended-spice,easy-to-cook,herbs,essential-products,horeca-products,upwas-products' | split: ',' -%}
  {%- if known_categories contains primary_handle -%}
    {%- assign sound_key = primary_handle -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- assign sound_override = product.metafields.custom.sound_clip.value -%}

  <button
    type="button"
    class="vishesh-sound-btn"
    data-sound-key="{{ sound_key }}"
    {%- if sound_override != blank %}
      data-sound-src="{{ sound_override | prepend: 'sounds/' | asset_url }}"
    {%- endif %}
    aria-pressed="false"
    aria-label="Play sound"
    data-label-play="Play sound"
    data-label-stop="Stop sound"
  >
    {% comment %}
      Custom icon treatment, not a stock mute/volume glyph - matches the
      brand's own visual language: the idle state reuses the exact
      sparkle mark (✦) already used in the hero, purity-promise and
      bestsellers sections, and the playing state is a small masala-jar
      silhouette with a stagger of "flavour waves" (styled like a mini
      equaliser) rather than a generic speaker icon.
    {% endcomment %}
    {%- comment -%}
      Both states are a speaker cone, the conventional pattern: muted
      shows a slash, playing shows sound-wave arcs. The arcs keep the
      staggered animation the old equaliser bars had, so the button
      still reads as actively playing rather than just toggled.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <span class="vishesh-sound-btn__icon vishesh-sound-btn__icon--off" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <path d="M4 9.5h3.4L12 5.6v12.8L7.4 14.5H4Z" fill="currentColor"/>
        <path d="M16.5 9.5 21 14M21 9.5 16.5 14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
              stroke-linecap="round"/>
      </svg>
    </span>
    <span class="vishesh-sound-btn__icon vishesh-sound-btn__icon--on" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <path d="M4 9.5h3.4L12 5.6v12.8L7.4 14.5H4Z" fill="currentColor"/>
        <path class="vishesh-sound-btn__wave vishesh-sound-btn__wave--1"
              d="M15.2 9.6a3.6 3.6 0 0 1 0 4.8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
              stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <path class="vishesh-sound-btn__wave vishesh-sound-btn__wave--2"
              d="M18 7.6a7 7 0 0 1 0 8.8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
              stroke-linecap="round"/>
      </svg>
    </span>
  </button>
{%- endif -%}
